      "correct_answer": null,
      "explanation_text": "Area of the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}}+\\frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}}=1$ $\\begin{aligned} & \\text{is}\\pi|ab| \\\\ & a^{2}=25,b^{2}=\\lambda^{2} \\end{aligned}$ Area of the ellipse $\\frac{x^{2}}{25}+\\frac{b^{2}}{\\lambda^{2}}=1$ is $\\pi \\times 5 \\times |\\lambda|$ . $\\begin{aligned} \\Rightarrow & & 20\\pi & =5\\pi|\\lambda| \\\\ \\Rightarrow & & |\\lambda| & =4 \\\\ \\Rightarrow & & \\lambda & = \\pm 4 \\end{aligned}$",
